  {
   "id": "HgrX1K-2BAAJ",
   "from": "Melanie Montes",
   "author": "5f94295e0980aa5d",
   "date": "2017-01-23T15:57:01Z",
   "subject": "How do you see which individuals have been sorted into the same MLG using mlg.filter?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi, <div>I was wondering how you can see which individuals belong to which contracted mlg, as when I run <a href=\"http://mlg.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mlg.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480732022000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ATXbt3Pv55vHr5NAk1jH5\">mlg.id</a> after mlg.filter, it still shows the original (non-filtered) mlgs. </div><div><br></div><div>Also, in general is it reccommended to run mlg.filter before all other analyses? </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks! </div><div>Melanie </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "mCGERHO3BAAJ",
   "from": "Zhian Kamvar",
   "author": "d192ec4b1d416345",
   "date": "2017-01-23T16:11:01Z",
   "subject": "Re: [poppr] How do you see which individuals have been sorted into the same MLG using mlg.filter?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Hi Melanie,<div><br></div><div>Can you provide a minimal working example? From my end, this process works. Check to see if your genclone object shows that the MLGs represented are filtered (if it says &quot;contracted&quot; multilocus genotypes when you show the object). </div><div><br></div><div>Here&#39;s an example with the monpop data:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;overflow:auto;font-size:13px;padding:9.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:10px;line-height:1.42857;color:rgb(51,51,51);word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(245,245,245);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-top-left-radius:4px;border-top-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-right-radius:4px;border-bottom-left-radius:4px;font-variant-ligatures:normal\"><code style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">suppressPackageStartupMessages</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,0,0);font-weight:bold\">library</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">poppr</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">monpop</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mlg.filter</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">monpop</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">.Machine</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">$</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">double.eps</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">monpop</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; This is a genclone object</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; -------------------------</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; Genotype information:</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;    236 contracted multilocus genotypes</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;        (0) [t], (diss.dist) [d], (farthest) [a] </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;    694 haploid individuals</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;     13 codominant loci</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; Population information:</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;      1 stratum - Pop</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;     12 populations defined - </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; 7_09_BB, 26_09_BB, 26_09_FR, ..., 45_10_FR, 26_11_BB, 26_11_FR</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">length</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://mlg.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mlg.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480732029000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3otSXESyxApXU3CYZpSQdO\">mlg.id</a></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">monpop</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; [1] 236</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mll</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">monpop</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(221,17,68)\">&quot;original&quot;</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">monpop</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; This is a genclone object</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; -------------------------</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; Genotype information:</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;    264 original multilocus genotypes </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;    694 haploid individuals</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;     13 codominant loci</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; Population information:</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;      1 stratum - Pop</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt;     12 populations defined - </span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; 7_09_BB, 26_09_BB, 26_09_FR, ..., 45_10_FR, 26_11_BB, 26_11_FR</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">length</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"http://mlg.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mlg.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792480732029000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3otSXESyxApXU3CYZpSQdO\">mlg.id</a></span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">monpop</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(104,118,135)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">#&gt; [1] 264</span></code></pre><div>Hope that helps!</div></div><div>Zhian</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div>"
    ],
